<description>&lt;p&gt;Iraqi security forces have arrested an Iraqi duo suspected of plotting attacks on a synagogue in Germany and have foiled a smuggling attempt of 36,000 liters of crude oil in Kirkuk, while also discovering a breach in a pipeline there. Baghdad has closed two border crossings in the Kurdistan region with Syria and Iran and ordered a nationwide deployment to secure oil fields, prompting protests by families of terrorism victims over benefit cuts in Mosul and demands for jobs by petroleum engineering graduates in Kirkuk. President Al Zaidi has called for dialogue and constitutional commitment as Trump backs his efforts to assert state authority, and a former US diplomat has criticized the Erbil-Baghdad dispute. The UCDP recorded 396 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxPT2MxVEJYVHRnSDRQZzRETWUyMnlCYUJDTTVTVzNuenBwRkRKeTgxZnBDR0VUVWt4akRiYzdMSnc5Sk9PWTBUMy00UFNBeUxsU0F1T1dzcFM2QkFuYTJINzZ1WmJzYUxaZnJoM3U1Q1k3N1JjLXZyQ29TS3IwZ1EwQU0yaXVNcnk0Y3ZIWDFuSzlOekJjb0RyMzdBR1N6TXJITGtzM09PQ2s4Ujg?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Times of Israel&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE1GX3lDZUMzYWNfV2lGX1ktM0JGUFNKaVEteG16QTBEVmcyUWxvQl9JbFgxU1g5Z3NwS1ppVFRLdTJjcHBKUE96SHA4Z1QwcmdBSDlERzJGS0c?oc=5&quot;&gt;Ahram Online&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxPWVdKLW9Nb21CeUtzZzRZd1Q5RmwtdlZBdjJFNzZ3T0VGSUgwUl9lRkxRUjNSM25vc0ZfdWxfVEx2Ui1sVWZPSk92cHNlOVBnUlVSRWJUWVdnMzQzNFZVX2JIdzZ6SGtLRDE0T2tnaVFKRlMwTWY0TU5BOGNzaTRGanRMeWFJZVlJQUNvc21ocmtSWjg3U2l5T3NCeGo5dnR2TGdnT21YM3ZxYkhRUDFR?oc=5&quot;&gt;وكالة الانباء العراقية (واع)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixgFBVV95cUxOU0hM